RUN: mkdir -p %t.d
RUN: %PLC --constructors-only -c --fpic %S/interface_c_owner_lib.pli -o %t.d/ctors.o
RUN: cc -c -fPIC %S/interface_c_owner_lib.c -o %t.d/body.o
RUN: %COMPILE -i %S/interface_c_owner_lib.pli %S/interface_c_owner_main.st %t.d/ctors.o %t.d/body.o && %RUN | %CHECK %s
RUN: cc -shared %t.d/ctors.o %t.d/body.o -o %t.d/libgreet.so
RUN: %COMPILE -i %S/interface_c_owner_lib.pli %S/interface_c_owner_main.st -L%t.d -lgreet
RUN: env LD_LIBRARY_PATH=%STDLIBDIR:%t.d %t.out | %CHECK %s
RUN: sed -E 's/^(INTERFACE|FUNCTION_BLOCK) /{external} \1 /' %S/interface_c_owner_lib.pli > %t.d/external.pli
RUN: %PLC --constructors-only -c --fpic %t.d/external.pli -o %t.d/ctors_external.o
RUN: %COMPILE -i %t.d/external.pli %S/interface_c_owner_main.st %t.d/ctors_external.o %t.d/body.o && %RUN | %CHECK %s
RUN: %COMPILE %t.d/external.pli %S/interface_c_owner_main.st %t.d/ctors_external.o %t.d/body.o && %RUN | %CHECK %s

interface_c_owner_lib.c implements CGreeter, and --constructors-only generates
the constructors of interface_c_owner_lib.pli, also those of the IGreet
parameter types. The program includes interface_c_owner_lib.pli, so only the
constructors-only object may define these symbols. The program links the
objects directly, and then links the shared library built from them.

A C library can also mark its declarations {external}. --constructors-only
still generates all constructors for them, also those of the IGreet parameter
types, and the program links them, with the header included or compiled as
source.

